(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// The import system (PY5e; PYI-SPEC.md §9's single-file imports): import-name, import-from and"] [13 1 "// import-star, and builtins.__import__, after importlib._bootstrap's __import__, _gcd_import,"] [14 1 "// _find_and_load and _handle_fromlist. A module is found on sys.path (a package's submodules on its"] [15 1 "// __path__): DIR/NAME/__init__.py (a package), DIR/NAME.py, else DIR/NAME as a namespace package; its"] [16 1 "// source is compiled to the IR by the host (SetCompiler: the reader and arbace.python.compile) and run"] [17 1 "// as the module's body. The built-in modules are builtins and sys; the C modules of CPython are PY6's"] [18 1 "// Go ports (survey §6.6), so their import is a ModuleNotFoundError until then. importlib._bootstrap as"] [19 1 "// the import system itself (PYS12) is PY6's: no finders, loaders or specs yet (__spec__ is None)."] [21 1 "// builtinModuleNames are sys.builtin_module_names: every module the runtime makes (builtinModules', builtinModulesErr's),"] [22 1 "// with sys and builtins, sorted. Computed at first use, after every file's init registered its modules (PY6-core, queue"] [23 1 "// 200: a fixed list here missed the families' new modules, and importlib's BuiltinImporter then did not find them)."] [32 31 "// loaded on their first import (builtins_pyexpat_api.go)"] [43 1 "// builtinModules make the built-in modules other than builtins and sys, once per interpreter (their files'"] [44 1 "// init functions fill it: _string's builtins_string.go, _weakref's builtins_weakref.go)."] [47 1 "// builtinModulesErr are the built-in modules whose making may raise (those that run Python's machinery:"] [48 1 "// _ast's classes through type())."] [51 1 "// compileHook compiles a module's source text to the IR's text (arbace.python/ir-text); mode is \"exec\""] [52 1 "// or \"single\" (the REPL's). Any other result than a code object's map is an error \"Type: message\", or"] [53 1 "// \"incomplete\"