nce: the parse ends there, queue 228)."] [201 4 "// _PyPegen_number_token: a decimal literal over sys.set_int_max_str_digits's limit, which is the run's: the"] [202 4 "// reader records the digits of one past the lowest limit (p[1]) and the error's location"] [212 21 "// a compiler's warning: PyErr_ProgramTextObject's line"] [223 1 "// emitCompileWarnings is _PyErr_EmitSyntaxWarning for each of the compiler's warnings, in order:"] [224 1 "// warnings.warn_explicit(msg, SyntaxWarning, file, line); a SyntaxWarning a filter turns into an error becomes"] [225 1 "// the SyntaxError of its location, the compile's result."] [266 1 "// isIncomplete reports an interactive statement that needs more lines (codeop's incomplete input):"] [267 1 "// (PY7: a fresh _IncompleteInputError each time, isIncomplete tells it)"] [283 4 "// builtins.__import__ replaced: called as CPython's import_name calls it"] [320 4 "// a mapping's namespace (a dict subclass's, exec's mapping; queue 219): the names stored through it"] [334 1 "// builtinImportFn is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [337 1 "// isBuiltinImport is whether o is the runtime's builtins.__import__."] [340 1 "// builtinImport is __import__(name, globals=None, locals=None, fromlist=(), level=0)."] [379 1 "// importName is IMPORT_NAME (importlib's __import__): the module named, relative to globals' package by"] [380 1 "// level; with an empty fromlist the top-level package of the name, else the module with fromlist's"] [381 1 "// submodules imported."] [442 1 "// handleFromlist imports the submodules a package's fromlist names (_handle_fromlist)."] [475 5 "// _handle_fromlist: a missing submodule is skipped, unless sys.modules blocks it with None"] [486 1 "// importFrom is IMPORT_FROM: module.name, else the submodule module.name already in sys.modules (a"] [487 1 "// circular import), else an ImportError."] [519 3 "// import_from's shadowing messages (ceval.c, queue 223): the spec's file origin, else __file__"] [539 2 "// import_from's ImportError: name the module, path its file, name_from the name (PY6b's request)"] [548 1 "// importStar is IMPORT_STAR: __all__'s names, else the module's public names, into ns."] [597 1 "// packageOf is the package a relative import is relative to (import.c's resolve_name, _calc___package__):"] [598 1 "// __package__, checked against __spec__.parent; else __spec__.parent; else, with an ImportWarning, __name__"] [599 1 "// (itself for a package)."] [659 1 "// resolveName is _resolve_name: name relative to package by level."] [675 1 "// importModule is _gcd_import: the module of the absolute name, its parents imported first."] [739 1 "// importBuiltin makes the built-in module name and puts it in sys.modules (ok false when name is not one):"] [740 1 "// the runtime's own import of them, and _imp.create_builtin's under importlib (PY6b)."] [750 23 "// a module whose Go package the host loads on demand (pyexpat)"] [753 25 "// PY6d's R5: the built-in functions' __module__"] [769 1 "// findAndLoad finds the module child (fully name) in the directories of search and runs it."] [805 1 "// loadSource compiles a module's source file and runs it as name (a package when path is not nil)."] [855 1 "// notFound is ModuleNotFoundError(msg) for the module name (its .name, ImportError's attribute)."] [875 1 "// moduleDict is a module's namespace (a *Module's Dict), else nil."] [888 1 "// moduleName is a module's __name__, \"\" when it has none."] [904 1 "// modulePath is a module's __path__ (a package's), nil for a plain module."] [920 1 "// The runtime's import system seen by importlib (PY6a): sys.meta_path holds pyiFinder, whose find_spec imports"] [921 1 "// the module by the runtime's own finder (sys.path, packages, the built-in modules) and answers a"] [922 1 "// ModuleSpec of importlib._bootstrap whose loader hands that module over, so importlib.import_module and"] [923 1 "// importlib.util.find_spec work beside the import statement. importlib._bootstrap as the impor